  "definition": "Unit testing is a software testing practice in which individual units of source code \u2014 typically functions, methods, or classes \u2014 are exercised in isolation to verify that each behaves as specified. Tests are written as small, deterministic, automated checks that assert expected outputs for given inputs and run quickly as part of the development loop. The practice underpins refactoring confidence, regression protection, and continuous integration pipelines.",
